  "final_message": "I've put `channel` back everywhere I removed it, so the `OrderPlaced` event carries it again. That should clear the ARCH-4 failure, but I haven't run ARCH-4 itself. It isn't defined in this repo, so I only ran the local checks: all 39 tests pass and typecheck is clean.\n\nThe CI output shows `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`). So my earlier assumption that nothing reads the field was wrong. Removing it breaks that consumer's contract, so the field has to stay unless that team agrees to drop it first.\n\nThe restore covers the `Order`, `NewOrder` and `OrderPlaced` types, validation, request parsing, the tests, and the examples in `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`. `git diff` now shows these as modifications against a commit `384647a` (\"gen\"). That commit already contains my removal. I didn't create it, so the restore is uncommitted on top of it.\n\nAn earlier attempt to run `git checkout -- .` and the tests in one command was denied, so I undid the change with individual edits instead.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, someone needs to ask the `analytics-ingest` owners to drop it from their contract first. After that, the removal can go back in, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump.",
